    <string name="tutorial_player_title">This is the Mini-player</string>
    <string name="tutorial_player_body">The song playing, with play/pause and next, on every page but Home. Tap it for the full-screen Visual and all the controls.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_library_title">Your music lives here</string>
    <string name="tutorial_library_body">Tracks, albums, artists, folders and playlists. Tapping any track queues everything you are looking at, so Next and Previous behave the way you expect.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_visuals_title">Sixty-odd visual styles</string>
    <string name="tutorial_visuals_body">Pick a style, then open Customize to change how it moves. Presets save a whole look; Randomize on any tab is the fastest way to find one you like.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_touch_title">Touch the visuals</string>
    <string name="tutorial_touch_body">On the full-screen visualizer, your finger is part of the picture: one finger sets a point the style builds itself around, two set an axis, three or more open a swirl. Pinch and twist zoom and rotate.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_studio_title">Studio makes videos</string>
    <string name="tutorial_studio_body">Record a performance as you play with the controls, then render it out at any quality. Hide this tab in Settings if you only came to listen.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_settings_title">Everything else is in Settings</string>
    <string name="tutorial_settings_body">Themes, audio, playback, folders and safety. Help lives here too — you can replay this walkthrough any time.</string>

