    <!-- Settings > Help -->
    <string name="help_tutorial_group">Walkthrough</string>
    <string name="help_tutorial_body">A short tour of the Player, Library, Visuals and Studio. It navigates the app as it goes, so you see the real thing.</string>
    <string name="help_tutorial_start">Start the walkthrough</string>
    <string name="help_tutorial_replay">Replay the walkthrough</string>
    <string name="help_tutorial_on_first_run">Offer it on a fresh install</string>
    <string name="help_topics_group">How things work</string>
    <string name="help_topic_library">Library and folders</string>
    <string name="help_topic_library_body">Geode reads the audio Android already indexes. If you keep music somewhere it does not look — an SD card, or Downloads — add that folder in Settings › Folders.</string>
    <string name="help_topic_visuals">Styles, presets and Customize</string>
    <string name="help_topic_visuals_body">A style is the renderer; a preset is a style plus every control around it. Customize hides controls a style cannot use, so an empty section means that style ignores it rather than that something is broken.</string>
    <string name="help_topic_touch">Touch on the visualizer</string>
    <string name="help_topic_touch_body">Every style reads where your finger is and means something by it — a vanishing point, a spawn point, a place the geometry reaches toward. Pinch and twist map onto the real Zoom and Rotation controls, so a gesture you like is saved with the preset.</string>
    <string name="help_topic_safety">Flashing and motion</string>
    <string name="help_topic_safety_body">Nothing on screen can flash more than three times a second. That limit lives in the engine, covers exported video as well as the screen, and is always on — there is no switch for it and nothing to turn on. Settings › Behavior › Visual safety adds one choice on top: “Slow the motion down”, which eases movement, shake, drift and rotation if motion rather than flashing is what affects you.</string>
    <string name="help_topic_performance">If it runs hot or stutters</string>
    <string name="help_topic_performance_body">The engine already lowers its own quality when the device heats up. The Detail control on the marched styles is the biggest single lever you have, and lowering it costs less than you would expect.</string>

